#. module: alc_eshop_cms
#: model:alc.eshop.cms.page,content:alc_eshop_cms.alc_eshop_cms_page_about-us
msgid ""
"\n"
"<h1>About us?</h1>\n"
"<p>Alcyon, the leader in the distribution of medicines for animals, food and equipment, was created by and for vets, in order to provide them with the best solutions in conducting their daily practice.</p>\n"
"<h2>Alcyon is guided by a single strategy: fostering and strengthening the veterimary profession</h2>\n"
"<p>At the level of the ALCYON group, more than 5,000 practising vets are both our customers and our shareholders. ALCYON’s logistical knowhow is at your service on a daily basis! With Alcyon, you benefit from the country’s most extensive product range. Being in the profession ourselves, we understand where you’re coming from!</p>\n"
"<h2>Developing services tailored to your expectations</h2>\n"
"<p>Alcyon is attuned to your expectations. We are offering you a set of services devised to make your daily life easier and allow you to evolve in better conditions.</p>\n"
"<h2>Achieve excellence</h2>\n"
"<p>In order to be effective, we need to be skilled. That is why your Alcyon teams receive regular training in order to ensure the best service. This is an essential point in our relationship with you: reception, information, order, after-sales service, etc.</p>\n"
"<h2> </h2>\n"
"<h1>100% VETERINARY</h1>\n"
"<h2>Alcyon is your company - it is the only distribution company that is 100% owned by vets</h2>\n"
"<p>The Board of Directors is made up of 12 practising colleagues. They share your everyday experience and make sure that Alcyon meets your expectations.</p>\n"
"<h2> </h2>\n"
"<h1>Alcyon’s values</h1>\n"
"<h2>Authenticity</h2>\n"
"<p>Our company’s articles of association, which constitute our guarantee of independence, provide that only veterinary practitioners can hold shares. Alcyon is and always will be a veterinary distribution company in the service of the profession. ALCYON is there to protect the sector. Our investment is not speculative. Our customers are our shareholders! YOU too can become an ALCYON shareholder. Find out about it!</p>\n"
"<h2>Performance</h2>\n"
"<p>Both economically and logistically wise.</p>\n"
"<p>Economically because your company needs to release the necessary funds for maintaining and developing the necessary tools for meeting your needs.</p>\n"
"<p>Logistically because every day each of our staff members will make all of our products and services needed for the most efficient and harmonious practice of your science of healing available to you precisely when and where you need them.</p>\n"
"<h2>Ingenuity</h2>\n"
"<p>In order to be effective, we need to be skilled, inventive and creative! That is why your ALCYON teams receive regular training in order to ensure the best service and best response to your needs. Our teams needs to constantly evolve, meet and anticipate the very least of your expectations and develop adequate services.</p>\n"
"<h2>Adaptability</h2>\n"
"<p>ALCYON’s size favours adaptability. We can react very quickly to deal with any situation. We don’t need to follow the arbitrary regulations of big groups more ruled by short-term profits and stock-exchange results than by their customers’ satisfaction.</p>\n"
"<h2> </h2>\n"
"<h1>Alcyon is the sole distributeur by and for veterinary practitioners</h1>\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: alc_eshop_cms
#: model:alc.eshop.cms.page,content:alc_eshop_cms.alc_eshop_cms_page_born-to-share
msgid ""
"\n"
"<h1>Born to share</h1>\n"
"<h2>Showroom</h2>\n"
"<p>Our Villiers-le-Bouillet premises are designed to respond as efficiently as possible to our profession’s logistical challenges, but we also wanted to be able to receive our clients with the same degree of efficiency. Our showroom welcomes vets who would like to place their orders directly on-site and more generally all vets who take part in seminars and conferences. Each year, the general meeting allows our many shareholders (over 100 at this time) to visit our showroom. Here you will find various equipment and work instruments, which you can compare and analyse in order to meet your needs as effectively as possible.</p>\n"
"<h2>Our training courses</h2>\n"
"<p>Created by and for veterinary surgeons, ALCYON Belux will assist you throughout your career. ALCYON Belux is associated with carefully chosen partners to assist you with your training. These partners may either be directly linked with you at your work or connected by a series of peripheral services allowing you to devote a maximum of time and energy to your passion - your veterinary work!</p>\n"
"<p>Please do not hesitate to communicate your needs in terms of company set-up, finances, marketing, etc. ALCYON Belux will always try to find you the training course that suits you best and provides you with the maximum added value.</p>\n"
"<p><strong>Please do not hesitate to communicate your requests via your delegates:</strong></p>\n"
"<p><strong>Muriel DEGROOTE</strong><br/> Verviers, Liège, Namur, Charleroi, Mons<br/> Tel. : 0471 / 78 25 25<br/> Email : <a href=\"mailto:muriel.degroote@alcyonbelux.be\">muriel.degroote@alcyonbelux.be</a></p>\n"
"<p><strong>Raymond PIRARD</strong><br/> South and East Wallonia<br/> Tel. : 0475 / 36 57 24<br/> Email : <a href=\"mailto:raymond.pirard@alcyonbelux.be\">raymond.pirard@alcyonbelux.be</a></p>\n"
"<p><strong>Patricia LEVAN</strong><br/> Western and Eastern Flanders<br/> Tel. : 0476 / 64 53 63<br/> E-mail : <a href=\"mailto:patricia.levan@alcyonbelux.be\">patricia.levan@alcyonbelux.be</a></p>\n"
"<p><strong>Patricia DERYCKE</strong><br/> Brussels, Walloon Brabant, Hainaut<br/> Tel. : 0486 / 63 53 65<br/> E-mail : <a href=\"mailto:patricia.derycke@alcyonbelux.be\">patricia.derycke@alcyonbelux.be</a></p>\n"
"<h2>Our Seminars</h2>\n"
"<p>Would you like to organise a course, conference or product demonstration for vets? Are you looking for a completely equipped and well located room? The Alcyon seminar room is exactly what you need.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: alc_eshop_cms
#: model:alc.eshop.cms.page,content:alc_eshop_cms.alc_eshop_cms_page_chronology-crazy-dream
msgid ""
"\n"
"<h1>Chronology of a rather crazy dream</h1>\n"
"<p>It could all be summed up by a quote from Dom Helder CAMARA: “When we are dreaming alone, it’s only a dream. When we are dreaming with others, it’s the beginning of reality. Shared utopia is the province of history.”</p>\n"
"<p>It all began back in the nineteen nineties. In response to particular circumstances, a few kamikaze vets decided to set up a veterinary group following a model that had already existed in France for over 20 years. Two cooperatives were born, PROLIPHARM and PROLIMAT. They were joined by around fifty practising vets.</p>\n"
"<p>The goal was simple: to create a professional tool by and for veterinary practitioners with a view to anticipating developments in the profession and protecting the profession’s economic future.</p>\n"
"<p>Our colleagues, Eric BASLEER, a practitioner in Heure le Romain and Michel DANS, who decided to give up his rural practice in Fexhe le Haut Clocher, were entrusted respectively with the presidency and the daily management. PROLIPHARM rapidly took on a significant role in the distribution of pharmaceutical products in the Liège province.</p>\n"
"<p>In 1996, the general management was entrusted to Dr. Pierre VAN THEMSCHE and the business management was handed over to Jean-Pierre CULOT.</p>\n"
"<p>That same year, SOBELVET became the majority shareholder of COPHARDEL, a joint-stock corporation undertaking activities that were theoretically similar to ours.</p>\n"
"<p>Following an action brought before the Belgian Association of Veterinary Practitioners, a mixed appeal board issued a ground-breaking judgement for us and vets, confirming that being a shareholder in a company like SOBELVET did not conflict with the code of ethics.</p>\n"
"<p>In 1997, SOBELVET absorbed Cophardel’s activities and transferred them to Seraing along with the veterinary activities of the pharmacy CONCORDE situated in the Namur region.</p>\n"
"<p>Initiatives were taken in a context of partnership with the veterinary world (parliamentary questions, seminar on veterinary medication, molecules and orphan diseases, etc.). We committed ourselves by a contract to meet the profession’s needs.</p>\n"
"<p>In 2001, we innovated, making our first veterinary website available to our colleagues with an e-commerce section online. At the end of the year, we resumed the veterinary pharmacy activities of EXIMPHARM in Bastogne, managed by our colleague Guy MALDAGUE.</p>\n"
"<p>In February 2002, the company was nominated as one of the “Gazelles 2002” [companies distinguished by their growth and dynamism] by the weekly journal TRENDS TENDANCES. It was nominated again the following year. We were given a third distinction in 2006 and several times more since then. In October 2003, we were proud to inaugurate the extension of our building in Seraing.</p>\n"
"<p>In 2003, 4 French veterinary distribution cooperatives, COVELY, VETARVOR, CAVEGAT and SAVENOR merged to form ALCYON France. The group ALCYON was born and shares in SOBELVET that had previously been held by SAVENOR were transferred into a key holding in ALCYON INTERNATIONAL, as were the shares of the Italian subsidiary COVEL'ITALIA held by COVELY.</p>\n"
"<p>In mid 2004, VETIPHAR, situated in Ath and founded and managed by our colleague, Guy DUQUESNE, was also absorbed. Two months later, the veterinary activities of the pharmacy HARDY in Amel (Amblève) were purchased and transferred to Seraing.</p>\n"
"<p>In January 2005, with the aim of harmonising at European level, SOBELVET decided to change its name to ALCYON BELUX SA. The group Alcyon is positioned as the premier veterinary distribution unit with over 3,600 vets who are shareholders.</p>\n"
"<p>At the end of the year, we took over the veterinary activities of the BON AIR pharmacy in Anderlecht.</p>\n"
"<p>At the beginning of 2009, we innovated further in our sector by installing Voice Picking, a process whereby warehouse staff prepare your orders guided by an artificial computer voice. We are pursuing multiple objectives: as well as productivity gains, we want to ensure consistency in the traceability of products while improving the well-being of the workers when preparing them.</p>\n"
"<p>In July, we took over the limited-liability partnership VETICOM based in Tielt-Winge, which opened up ALCYON a bit more to the Flemish-speaking part of the country.</p>\n"
"<p>On 17 August, the much anticipated work of building lobbies, platforms and offices got underway at Villers le Bouillet. The work was certified by the AFMPS on Thursday 1 April 2010 and the very next day, which was the beginning of the Easter weekend, the transfer of all materials, offices and stocks from Seraing to Villers le Bouillet was started up. No less than 32 trailers were loaded up, unloaded and tidied away over those 4 days during which the whole ALCYON BELUX pitched in to guarantee the customers’ satisfaction, having everything ready for them on the first working day after Easter.</p>\n"
"<p>The official inauguration of the new premises, in the presence of the ministers Marcourt and Laruelle took place on 30 April 2011. The appointment also took place of a new general manager, Serge Wuestenberghs, the first manager who was not himself a vet but a civil engineer with a masters in business management. Pierre Van Themsche was able to embark on his well-earned retirement.</p>\n"
"<p>Armed with its partners and the group’s own strength, ALCYON keeps on developing new services and products in the service of its partner pharmacies. ALCYON is the sole wholesaler/ distributor to be 100% owned by vets and whose directors are all vets</p>\n"
"<p>This has allowed ALCYON to remain faithful to its values, which you also share - realism, transparency, innovation and collegiality - and its promises:</p>\n"
"<p>Creating an effective professional tool in the service of practitioners and ensuring the continued development of its economic activities.</p>\n"
"<p>Deserving your trust is what makes us strong.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: alc_eshop_cms
#: model:alc.eshop.cms.page,content:alc_eshop_cms.alc_eshop_cms_page_export
msgid ""
"\n"
"<h1>Export</h1>\n"
"<p>The legislation on medication in Europe does not allow the free circulation of medicines. On the other hand, as regards other products, such as over-the-counter drugs, nutrition and equipment of any kind, ALCYON Belux can help you in your choices and can supply you anywhere in the world.</p>\n"
"<p>Our terms and conditions of sale relating to exports are entirely specific to the country in question. Thank you in advance for contacting us in order to obtain an offer and find out the precise terms and conditions for delivery and payment.</p>\n"
"<p>ALCYON Belux has positioned itself as an exit point for the group vis-à-vis the world. Our exports cover numerous continents and countries such as, obviously, the bordering countries, Luxembourg, France etc. but also countries much further afield, like Hong-Kong, China, Saudi Arabia, Rwanda, Gabon, the Democratic Republic of Congo, etc.</p>\n"
"<p>Do send us your questions so that we can meet your needs.</p>\n"
"<p>The world is a village!</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: alc_eshop_cms
#: model:alc.eshop.cms.page,content:alc_eshop_cms.alc_eshop_cms_page_general-conditions
msgid ""
"\n"
"<h1>General conditions of sale</h1>\n"
"<p>The sale and delivery of goods and the provision of services under the conditions laid down in these general terms and conditions of sale apply only to customers established in Belgium. For other customers, the conditions of sale must be negotiated on a case-by-case basis with our Alcyon Belux Distribution Vétérinaire S.A. sales department (callcenter@alcyonbelux.be).</p>\n"
"<p>These general terms and conditions for the sale of goods or the provision of services apply exclusively to all orders placed with Alcyon Belux Distribution Veterinaire S.A (hereinafter Alcyon Belux) and shall take precedence over any other terms and conditions of sale, subject to provisions to the contrary in a written agreement.</p>\n"
"<p>The general terms and conditions of sale and delivery set out below, which are deemed known to and unreservedly accepted by the buyers, forms an integral part of each order/ purchase by the buyer. Any contrary or derogating conditions of purchase or any other restriction on the buyer in this connection shall be void and ineffective, unless we have expressly accepted it in writing.</p>\n"
"<p>By placing an order on a website, a natural or legal person is deemed to have accepted these terms and conditions of sale in their entirety. They can be accessed via the website at any time and, where applicable, prevail over any other version and over the customer’s own general or other terms and conditions of purchase.</p>\n"
"<h2>1. Offers and orders</h2>\n"
"<p>Our offers are not binding. The products are offered for sale within the limits of the stock available at the time the order is recorded at ALCYON Belux. We are only committed to the sale once the order has been confirmed. Performance will occur under the general terms and conditions of sale and delivery, with the buyer’s general terms and conditions of purchase being excluded.</p>\n"
"<p>Confirmations of orders, orders and verbal agreements shall only bind us when they are confirmed in writing or, in the absence of a written confirmation, where we fulfil the order unreservedly by sending goods and the invoice.</p>\n"
"<h2>2. Deliveries</h2>\n"
"<p>Subject to express, written conditions, our delivery dates are provided solely for information purposes and are not binding on us. They shall be extended in the case of a delay on the buyer’s part in sending the necessary documents and information for the proper execution of the sale, even if the buyer is not directly answerable for this delay. Even if there is an express agreement concerning the delivery deadlines, cases of force majeure entitle us to cancel any delivery or order, in full or in part, or to suspend its execution without prior notice and without any compensation for the buyer.</p>\n"
"<p>We deliver the products to the delivery address agreed in our agreements prior to the start of our trading relationship. We reserve the right to choose the nature and mode of dispatch. Additional costs, incurred due to the buyer’s special requests concerning dispatch or delivery, will be borne by the latter.</p>\n"
"<p>Due to the economic conditions, from 03/14/2022, a fee of 2€ excluding VAT will be charged per delivery. For all orders with an amount less than 150€ excl. VAT, surcharges and miscellaneous contributions, a flat rate contribution of 10.50€ excl. VAT will be charged for delivery costs. Any orders to be delivered outside of Belgium require a written agreement concerning delivery modes and charges.</p>\n"
"<h2>3. Payment</h2>\n"
"<p>Subject to written provisions to the contrary, our invoices are payable within 7 days following the invoice date without any discounts or reductions. VAT as well as any other taxes, duties, fees or any other payments imposed by an authority in relation to the execution of the order shall be borne by the buyer.</p>\n"
"<p>Any sum that remains unpaid on the due date will lawfully give rise to default interest calculated on the basis of the applicable interest rate of the Banque Nationale, increased by 1%, without the need for a prior notice period. Moreover, the amount will be increased by a one-off compensation payment of 10%, with a minimum of €40 per invoice.</p>\n"
"<p>If the customer is considered a consumer pursuant to Law 6 April 2010 regarding market practices and the protection of the consumer, the aforesaid penalty clause will also be applicable to Alcyon S.A. if it has not fulfilled its own contractual obligations (reciprocity clause).</p>\n"
"<p>Payments are deemed made one we have actual and definitive access to the sums in question.</p>\n"
"<h2>4. Retention of ownership</h2>\n"
"<p>The products delivered remain owned by Alcyon Belux until full and effective payment has occurred, on a definitive and binding basis, in respect of all sums owed to us.</p>\n"
"<h2>5. Returning goods</h2>\n"
"<p>In principle, we do not accept returns of our goods and products. In exceptional and very particular cases described in points 5.1 to 5.4 below, we are, however ready to take back certain goods or products. In all cases, the costs of returning goods will be borne by the buyer.</p>\n"
"<p>5.1 Only return requests reported within 48 hours or receipt of the goods will be considered. The request must be accompanied by a copy of the dispatch note returning the products under dispute.</p>\n"
"<p>5.2 The products must be in perfect condition (original packaging, not torn, with no writing and/or additional labels, etc.) and accompanied by their accessories.</p>\n"
"<p>5.3. Products sold as part of a promotion must be returned under the business regulations set our above. The return will automatically invalidate the special conditions and lead to additional billing.</p>\n"
"<p>5.4. Products are returned under their terms and conditions of sale (price and discount). However, Alcyon Belux reserves the right to use 90% of the return sum to cover administrative and logistical fees.</p>\n"
"<p>5.5. The following cannot be returned:</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>products whose expiry date was indicated as tight,</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>products subject to compliance with strict preservation conditions (cold chain),</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>specially ordered products, precursors and “spin-off” products.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p>Delivery errors that can be attributed to ALCYON Belux will always be taken into consideration and the products will be credited without charge in compliance with points 5.1 and 5.2.</p>\n"
"<h2>6. Complaints</h2>\n"
"<p>Our products are considered to have been approved at latest 7 calendar days after their delivery to the agreed delivery address, save a specific, detailed claim communicated to us before the expiry of this term by email, fax or registered letter. Approval covers all visible defects, i.e. all those that can be detected by a diligent and competent purchaser at the time of the delivery or within the following 7 calendar days by a careful and serious inspection, including those relating to the product's characteristics and quantities.</p>\n"
"<p>Goods in respect of which a complaint has been made can only be sent back with our prior, express agreement and in their original packaging.</p>\n"
"<p>The complaint itself does not release the buyer from his or her payment obligation.</p>\n"
"<h2>7. Confidentiality and privacy</h2>\n"
"<p>All the personal details you send for the purposes of the order and its processing will be confidential and will not be communicated to third parties, save for the purpose of processing your payment.</p>\n"
"<p>In accordance with Belgian law of 8 December 1992 on the protection of privacy in the processing of personal details, as amended by the law of 11 December 1998, you have the right to access (communication of data) and rectify (correction of errors) your personal details. Our details are indicated in the legal notice, and a contact form is available on this site.</p>\n"
"<h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>\n"
"<p>The entire contents of the website (illustrations, photos, videos, descriptions, trade marks, etc.) are owned by Alcyon Belux and its co-contractors and partners. Any full or partial reproduction by any means whatsoever on any medium of any kind shall be subject to Alcyon Belux’ express, prior authorisation.</p>\n"
"<p>All goods sold by Alcyon Belux are protected by Belgian and international law concerning intellectual property and copyright. Illicit appropriation and reproduction by the user will be pursued under criminal law. Alcyon Belux can in no case be held liable for the violation by the User of rights held by third parties, committed by virtue of the User’s activities on the website.</p>\n"
"<h2>9. Applicable law and jurisdiction</h2>\n"
"<p>The contract concluded by the parties is governed by Belgian legislation.</p>\n"
"<p>Any disputes come under the sole jurisdiction of the justice of peace in the county or the courts in the district in which Alcyon Belux’ head office is situated.</p>\n"
"<h2>10. Invalid conditions</h2>\n"
"<p>If certain clauses of these general terms and conditions of sale and delivery are invalid, this will not affect the legitimacy of the other clauses or parts thereof. The parties must replace an invalid provision by one that is valid and that comes as close as possible to achieving the economic objective of the invalid provision.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

